Direct product-level repro of fm_procevent_private_directory_valid on a symlinked
vs resolved path, comparing base commit 355f46f against target commit 73617bf.

/tmp is itself a symlink to /private/tmp on this macOS host, so this mirrors the
$TMPDIR -> /private/var/... shape described in the diagnosis without depending on
$TMPDIR itself.

Setup:
  mkdir -p /tmp/repro-root/real/dir && chmod 700 /tmp/repro-root/real/dir
  ln -s /tmp/repro-root/real /tmp/repro-root/link
  DIR_LINKED=/tmp/repro-root/link/dir             # crosses the /tmp -> /private/tmp symlink
  DIR_RESOLVED=/private/tmp/repro-root/real/dir   # already physical

Command (run against each checkout):
  bash -c '. bin/fm-pr-lib.sh; . bin/fm-procevent-lib.sh
    fm_procevent_private_directory_valid "$DIR_LINKED" 1 && echo accepted || echo rejected
    fm_procevent_private_directory_valid "$DIR_RESOLVED" 1 && echo accepted || echo rejected'

=== BASE (355f46f) ===
symlinked path (/tmp/repro-root/link/dir): rejected
resolved path  (/private/tmp/repro-root/real/dir): accepted

=== TARGET (73617bf, this worktree) ===
symlinked path (/tmp/repro-root/link/dir): accepted
resolved path  (/private/tmp/repro-root/real/dir): accepted

Conclusion: at base, the same directory is rejected via its symlinked spelling
and accepted via its resolved spelling -- exactly the defect described in the
user intent ("the same directory was rejected via its symlinked path and
accepted via its resolved path"). At target, both spellings are accepted,
because fm_procevent_private_directory_valid now compares the physical
location against fm_procevent_path_physical_expected() (ancestors resolved,
leaf appended verbatim) instead of the purely lexical normalization.
